statement:
Let $(A,\mathfrak m)$ be a nonzero commutative Noetherian local ring, meaning a commutative Noetherian ring with unique maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ [def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring], and let $\kappa=A/\mathfrak m$. Let $K\in D(A)$ [def-weil-abstract-derived-category] be a normalized algebraic dualizing complex, meaning that $K$ is isomorphic to a bounded complex of injective $A$-modules [def-sp-injective-resolutions], every $H^j(K)$ is finitely generated, the scalar-action map $A[0]	o R\operatorname{Hom}_A(K,K)$ is an isomorphism, and $R\operatorname{Hom}_A(\kappa[0],K)\cong\kappa[0]$ in $D(A)$; here $R\operatorname{Hom}_A$ is the derived internal Hom on the one-object ringed site [def-pur-derived-internal-hom]. Let $M$ be a nonzero finitely generated $A$-module [def-weil-finitely-generated-module]. For $i\in\mathbf Z$ put $E^i=H^i(R\operatorname{Hom}_A(M[0],K))$. Let $\operatorname{Supp}_A(M)$ be the set of primes $\mathfrak q$ with $M_{\mathfrak q}
e0$ [def-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime], and let $d_M$ be its dimension, the supremum of the lengths of strict chains of primes all lying in $\operatorname{Supp}_A(M)$ [def-weil-pbc-krull-dimension-ring]. Then: (1) if $d_M$ is finite, $E^i=0$ for $i<-d_M$ and for $i>0$; (2) $\operatorname{depth}_{\mathfrak m}(M)$ [def-weil-pbc-depth] is finite and equals the smallest integer $t\geq0$ for which $E^{-t}
e0$. In particular, $E^{-\operatorname{depth}_{\mathfrak m}(M)}
e0$ and $E^{-t}=0$ whenever $0\leq t<\operatorname{depth}_{\mathfrak m}(M)$.

proof.text:
