e0$. This completes the induction. Apply it with $T=M$ and its finite depth from Step 1. For $0\le t<\operatorname{depth}(M)=n$, the inequality $-t>-n$ gives $E^{-t}=0$, and $E^{-n}
e0$. Hence $n$ is precisely the smallest nonnegative integer $t$ with $E^{-t}
e0$, which proves clause (2).
